course: dictionary
lesson: 15673
title: Thus: so, like this, and so far
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Thus» is a formal word, the kind you find in books, reports and exams. It usually means «so» or «therefore»: one thing happens, and thus another thing follows. «The shop was closed, thus we bought our bread at the station.» The word thus joins the reason to the result.
explain: Thus can also mean «in this way» or «like this». «Hold the bat thus, with your hands close together.» Here thus points to how something is done, so you can copy it.
explain: Read the words around thus to check which meaning fits. Swap in «so» and see if the sentence still makes sense. If it does, thus means «so» or «as a result».
fact: Thus means «so», «therefore» or «as a result».
fact: Thus can also mean «in this way» or «like this».
fact: «Thus far» means «so far» or «until now».
fact: Thus is a formal word, so it often sounds grand or old-fashioned in stories.
fact: In maths and science, thus joins a result to the working or reason that led to it.
exercise: «The bus was late, thus we missed the start of the film.» What does thus mean here? | *So, as a result | Under the table | Happily, with a smile | In a hurry, very fast
exercise: «Fold the paper thus, then press the crease flat.» What does thus mean here? | Far away | Very loudly | *In this way, like this | Before lunch
exercise: The phrase «thus far» means what? | *So far, until now | At the end of the day | Tomorrow morning | Very far away
test: «The rain fell all night, thus the match was cancelled.» What does thus show? | The rain was warm | A dance started early | *The result of the rain: the match was cancelled because of it | The match was won by the home team
test: Ben wrote, «Add 5 to both sides, thus x = 9.» What does thus tell you? | *x = 9 is the result of the working before it | The sides of the sum are silly | x is a very big number | Add nothing at all
exam: Which sentence uses thus to mean «like this»? | He was late, thus he ran to school | *Hold the racket thus and swing it hard | The fire was hot, thus we moved back | Thus far the day has been fun
